---
source: crates/unblock-cli/tests/help_snapshots.rs
expression: "help(&[\"migrate\", \"--help\"])"
---
Ensure the workspace database schema is current and report the from→to delta (FR-16).

Migration is FORWARD-ONLY and it MOVES the on-disk schema version, so an OLDER `unblock` meeting a database this command has migrated refuses to open it (exit 2, `SCHEMA_MISMATCH`) instead of misreading a shape it does not understand — upgrade every binary that shares this workspace. The on-disk schema is not part of the version-stable CLI surface (D35), so this direction ships in a patch release; it is stated here rather than left to be inferred from silence (D46 clause (8)).

Usage: unblock migrate [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --dir <DIR>
          The explicit workspace `.unblock/` directory (no walk-up; `--dir` > `UNBLOCK_DIR`, MF-2)
          
          [env: UNBLOCK_DIR=]

      --actor <ACTOR>
          The actor override (`--actor` > `UNBLOCK_ACTOR`, FORK-4)
          
          [env: UNBLOCK_ACTOR=]

  -o, --output <FORMAT>
          The output format for rendered reports (`json|robot|plain|csv|markdown`). NO clap `env` — `UNBLOCK_OUTPUT_FORMAT` is owned by config's strict env layer for workspace commands; the flag still forwards so `--flag > env` holds (spine §5b)

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase verbosity (`-v` INFO, `-vv` DEBUG, `-vvv+` TRACE). Logs go to stderr only (NFR-14)

  -q, --quiet
          Suppress all but error-level diagnostics (`-q`). Overrides `-v`

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
